<note xml:id="n116" pname="a" oct="4" dur="2" dots="1">
<verse n="1"><syl>name!</syl></verse></note>
<rest xml:id="r117" dur="4"/>
</layer></staff>
<harm staff="1" tstamp="1" place="above">A♭</harm>
<harm staff="1" tstamp="2" place="above">D♭/A♭</harm>
<harm staff="1" tstamp="4" place="above">A♭</harm>
</measure>
</section></score></mdiv></body>
<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>Call upon the name of Jesus, and you will be saved,</l><l>O Lord Jesus, hallelujah, nevermore enslaved!</l><l>We may take salvation’s cup by calling on the Lord;</l><l>Salvation from a host of things does His dear name afford.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>To the Lord, the Jew, the Greek and everyone’s the same;</l><l>He is rich unto all men that call upon His name.</l><l>O Lord Jesus, what a joy to call and really live;</l><l>When breathing in Thy name, what pleasure Thou</l><l>to us dost give.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>In the God of our salvation we may take delight,</l><l>Calling on His name at all times, though in bliss or blight.</l><l>I will call upon His name as long as I shall live,</l><l>Because He has inclined His ear, and grace so full does give.</l></lg>
<lg label="5."><l>We will call upon the Lord, who’s worthy of our praise;</l><l>Thus our grateful hearts in worship we to Him may raise.</l><l>We are those who call upon His name in every place</l><l>With all the saints who from a pure heart call and taste His grace.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
